 wait. Let me reconsider whether to deviate from upstream at all. The user's third requirement: \"when I pass a PyJWK to decode functions and don't explicitly specify the algorithms parameter, I want the system to automatically use the algorithm associated with that JWK... I want these improvements to work consistently across all decode operations, including both jwt.decode() and jwt.decode_complete()\".\n\nIf I don't touch api_jwt.py's guard, then `jwt.decode(token, jwk)` fails — clearly violating the user's requirement. The user explicitly stated `jwt.decode()` should accept the PyJWK instance. So deviation is needed. But wait... let me double-check that module-level jwt.decode with PyJWK and no algorithms actually fails in upstream 2.9.0 — maybe I'm missing that `jwt.decode` module-level function maps to api_jws? Let me check jwt/__init__.py.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee8da7a8-0bbe-4466-be9c-5dd0aa2755a7","uuid":"0b7b9cd1-b141-470a-a84d-4caaf6e6e438","timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:42:55.528Z","request_id":"gen-1788507728-TMAIbkmtCNxCAsn9IXCs"}
