{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788508060-Tssj9LnBqAdtjHBk1rVX","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"mypy isn't installed, and grep found no \"PyJWK\" in docs/api.rst — so api.rst doesn't document PyJWK at all (probably references elsewhere). Let me check what's in api.rst quickly and whether docs build exists. Since api.rst has no PyJWK section, there's nothing to update there. (Upstream didn't either.)\n\nNow, the docs have a `docs/faq.rst`? Not relevant.\n\nLet me double check there are no other callers of `_verify_signature` or places that pass key positionally where a PyJWK might break — e.g., `jwks_client.py` uses PyJWK; `PyJWKClient.get_signing_key_from_jwt` returns PyJWK. Tests pass.\n\nOne more potential issue: `jwt/api_jws.py` imports `PyJWK` from `.api_jwk`, and `jwt/api_jwk.py` imports `get_default_algorithms` from `.algorithms`. No cycle. But wait — `jwt/algorithms.py` imports? Let me confirm no cycle: algorithms imports from .exceptions, .utils, .warnings — fine.\n\nAlso check `jwt/jwks_client.py` — does it import api_jws? It imports PyJWK from .api_jwk. Fine.\n\nEverything passes the test suite (264 passed, including new tests).\n\nNow — one design question to revisit: in `_verify_signature`, when `key` is a PyJWK AND explicit `algorithms` is provided, we use `key.Algorithm` and `key.key` — i.e., the JWK's own algorithm object, not `get_algorithm_by_name(alg)`. If the header alg is e.g. \"HS256\" and the JWK alg is \"HS256\" and algorithms=[\"HS256\"], alg_obj = key.Algorithm (an HMACAlgorithm instance) — equivalent behavior. Edge: if a user registered a custom algorithm instance in the PyJWS and passed algorithms=[\"CUSTOM\"] with a JWK whose alg is \"HS256\"... then header alg CUSTOM wouldn't be in algorithms → InvalidAlgorithmError. Consistent with security posture.\n\nWhat about `PyJWS(options={\"verify_signature\": False})` with PyJWK? Guard skipped; `_verify_signature` not called. Fine.\n\nAlso: `decode_complete` with `key=PyJWK` and `verify_signature: False` in options and no algorithms — passes guard, no verification. Good.\n\nAnother subtle check — `algorithms` parameter validated at api_jwt level with `not algorithms and not isinstance(key, PyJWK)`. What if `key` is a `PyJWKSet`? Not supported — PyJWKSet has no `.key`; decode would fail in _verify_signature... Actually with algorithms provided and key=PyJWKSet: `isinstance(key, PyJWK)` False → guard raises only if algorithms missing; with algorithms provided, `_verify_signature` would call `alg_obj.prepare_key(PyJWKSet)` → prepare_key raises InvalidKeyError probably. Same as upstream. Not in scope.\n\nType annotation nuance: in `api_jws.decode`/`decode_complete`, `key: AllowedPublicKeys | PyJWK | str | bytes` — PyJWK imported at runtime, good for `from __future__ import annotations` (annotations lazy anyway).\n\nNow, the final verification of the whole feature set was done. Let me also run a quick sanity check that `import jwt` has no circular-import issue when importing submodules directly in different orders:\n\npython -c \"import jwt.api_jwt; import jwt.api_jws\" and \"python -c \"from jwt.api_jws import PyJWS\"\" (which triggers api_jwk import).\n\nAlso run the complete test suite one final time (done). And compile check on docs rst? Let me at least verify the CHANGELOG.rst is valid RST with docutils if available.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee8da7a8-0bbe-4466-be9c-5dd0aa2755a7","uuid":"ed61b32c-cf44-40fe-99e3-068c6455ec18","timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:48:09.536Z","request_id":"gen-